ter for ai  and they're doing it with an arm-based  grace cpu  this is huge for the x86 versus arm  battle  proving to consumers and companies that  arm is now the way to go  for the future of data processing and  everyone knows  that intel is unfortunately sticking  with x86  now as far as nvidia's roadmap they  announced that for the time being  they will include both x86 and arm based  products  every year and both of the architectures  will be able to use and support their  nvidia gpus  so just like apple nvidia is still going  to support x86  while they're transitioning to arm but  of course  we all know that at some point in the  future arm will take over  completely and nvidia will be perfectly  set  and ready to make the switch and we know  this for sure because of this quote  from jensen arm is the most popular cpu  in the world  for good reason it's super energy  efficient  it's open licensing model inspires a  world of innovators to create products  around it but here's by far  the most telling and important thing  that he said for the markets we serve  we can accelerate arms adoption this  means that intel is basically  screwed because nvidia's goal is quite  literally to accelerate the adoption of  arm and the faster this happens the more  screwed intel ultimately is  but wait there's more nvidia just  announced that they're partnering up  with amazon's aws graviton servers  which by the way are arm based to  improve  their geforce now gaming service and the  reason they're doing this  is because the graviton delivers  significantly better  price performance obviously because it's  arm-based  and going even further they announced an  arm machine  for scientific computing using the  ampere ultra  which of course is an arm-based chip and  then there's a system for edge  and enterprise which uses the marvel  oction  you guessed it arm-based but the next  announcement  is by far the most important to  consumers like you  and i and this is just insane nvidia